(5564804, 800971, 49773, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Melethia:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m trusting that Mr Zigomar Fantastic said nice things, since this is indeed a very delightful and enjoyable shot.  :-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hahaha, yeah, I was commenting on the bike''s brakes, haven''t seen a bike without gears in a while ;-) Just to add that this photo proves that it''s a photographer who is responsible for a good shot, not the camera.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Melethia: I''m trusting that Mr Zigomar Fantastic said nice things, since this is indeed a very delightful and enjoyable shot.  :-)   Hahaha, yeah, I was commenting on the bike''s brakes, haven''t seen a bike without gears in a while ;-) Just to add that this photo proves that it''s a photographer who is responsible for a good shot, not the camera. ', '2009-07-08 08:56:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5564809, 803321, 75849, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone for your comments. I must say I am disappointed this didn''t do better - was at least hoping for a 5.5. As I wrote above, this is a (blue) vase on its side and shot up close. Only the rim is in focus. I thought the b/w conversion gave it a bit o'' abstractness, but it looks like a lot of you scored it low because you couldn''t get what it was. Oh, well...</td>', 'Thanks everyone for your comments. I must say I am disappointed this didn''t do better - was at least hoping for a 5.5. As I wrote above, this is a (blue) vase on its side and shot up close. Only the rim is in focus. I thought the b/w conversion gave it a bit o'' abstractness, but it looks like a lot of you scored it low because you couldn''t get what it was. Oh, well...', '2009-07-08 08:59:42.000000', NULL, 0),
