(5566365, 802501, 31664, '<td valign="top">Again with the fantastic lion shot,  I wish I could come away from the Melbourne zoo with something half as good as this!  Excellent work.</td>', 'Again with the fantastic lion shot,  I wish I could come away from the Melbourne zoo with something half as good as this!  Excellent work.', '2009-07-09 01:23:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566372, 803448, 31664, '<td valign="top">Hey Kai,  well done on breaking that elusive 6.0 barrier!  Love the wheel</td>', 'Hey Kai,  well done on breaking that elusive 6.0 barrier!  Love the wheel', '2009-07-09 01:34:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566414, 803593, 96881, '<td valign="top">Posting a comment as it was asked for in the Forums......I didn''t vote in the FS, but here is a honest assessment of the photo.<br/> <br/>The photo lacks a wow! factor, an overall appeal that makes it stand out from the rest, and therefore attracts a lot of mid range votes.......<br/> <br/>The bubbles do nothing for the photo.  Some people mistook them for Lens flare, others for I don''t know what.  however, whatever they are, i feel they are just distracting elements that add nothing to the photo, and just add bright dots to attract the eye.<br/> <br/>Much of the picture is brick wall, plain and boring.  The brick doesn''t have the character, or the context in the shot, to add anything to it.<br/> <br/>The crop doesn''t work.  I would have cropped off the top, almost to the top of the flag.  The square crop does not work with this photo.  I also would have trimmed a little off the right.  By doing this, you move the couple further away from the centre of the picture, and closer to the right line of thirds.  therefore, this would have decentralised the couple, and helped balance the shot.  I would not have cropped the left, as any change to that removes much of the flag, changing it from a primary element into a distraction......Removing a small area from the bottom (to about 1 brick below the bottom of the flag) also gets rid of brick while emphasising the main elements.<br/> <br/>Lightening the Area on the top left (small area would remain) so that the shaddow is not as harsh would also have helped this image.  I also would have adjusted the Highlights to darken them, this then gives the bricks a righter feel, and removes the overall too light/overexposed feel the photo currently has due to the harsh light.<br/> <br/>Just my opinion, FWIW...............</td>', 'Posting a comment as it was asked for in the Forums......I didn''t vote in the FS, but here is a honest assessment of the photo. The photo lacks a wow! factor, an overall appeal that makes it stand out from the rest, and therefore attracts a lot of mid range votes....... The bubbles do nothing for the photo.  Some people mistook them for Lens flare, others for I don''t know what.  however, whatever they are, i feel they are just distracting elements that add nothing to the photo, and just add bright dots to attract the eye. Much of the picture is brick wall, plain and boring.  The brick doesn''t have the character, or the context in the shot, to add anything to it. The crop doesn''t work.  I would have cropped off the top, almost to the top of the flag.  The square crop does not work with this photo.  I also would have trimmed a little off the right.  By doing this, you move the couple further away from the centre of the picture, and closer to the right line of thirds.  therefore, this would have decentralised the couple, and helped balance the shot.  I would not have cropped the left, as any change to that removes much of the flag, changing it from a primary element into a distraction......Removing a small area from the bottom (to about 1 brick below the bottom of the flag) also gets rid of brick while emphasising the main elements. Lightening the Area on the top left (small area would remain) so that the shaddow is not as harsh would also have helped this image.  I also would have adjusted the Highlights to darken them, this then gives the bricks a righter feel, and removes the overall too light/overexposed feel the photo currently has due to the harsh light. Just my opinion, FWIW...............', '2009-07-09 02:22:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566426, 803593, 66515, '<td valign="top">Hi there, <br/> <br/>Personally, I really like this shot. To be honest its not going to be winner with the DPC crowd but it really tells a story quite well. I like how the bubbles and the rainbow flag frame the couple inside the window which acts as another frame. I guess in the land of "if only" I''d say if only that object in the top left wasn''t there. <br/> <br/>It would have been nice if the bubbles had been in focus but they are simply too far from the couple for that to happen. <br/> <br/>Really this is a great photojournalism shot in my opinion and I could honestly see it in a newspaper.</td>', 'Hi there,  Personally, I really like this shot. To be honest its not going to be winner with the DPC crowd but it really tells a story quite well. I like how the bubbles and the rainbow flag frame the couple inside the window which acts as another frame. I guess in the land of "if only" I''d say if only that object in the top left wasn''t there.  It would have been nice if the bubbles had been in focus but they are simply too far from the couple for that to happen.  Really this is a great photojournalism shot in my opinion and I could honestly see it in a newspaper.', '2009-07-09 02:56:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566446, 801875, 28882, '<td valign="top">this is beautiful.</td>', 'this is beautiful.', '2009-07-09 03:42:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566452, 801477, 28882, '<td valign="top">this is just amazing.  i think this should''ve been scored much higher.  38/407 is pretty good but there are some higher scoring ones that really don''t come close to this.</td>', 'this is just amazing.  i think this should''ve been scored much higher.  38/407 is pretty good but there are some higher scoring ones that really don''t come close to this.', '2009-07-09 03:52:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566453, 802698, 36371, '<td valign="top">absolutely stunning photo! Would make a beautiful poster for advertising that area! Straight into my favorites! Congrats!</td>', 'absolutely stunning photo! Would make a beautiful poster for advertising that area! Straight into my favorites! Congrats!', '2009-07-09 03:55:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566455, 803209, 28882, '<td valign="top">nice capture sir.  wonderful.</td>', 'nice capture sir.  wonderful.', '2009-07-09 03:55:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566456, 801796, 36371, '<td valign="top">beautiful! into my faves....</td>', 'beautiful! into my faves....', '2009-07-09 03:58:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566469, 803226, 5792, '<td valign="top">Congrats on a decent placing with a good photograph.<br/> <br/>After researching that region more after our hike I see there are many, many other equally fascinating places to photograph in the immediate area... I plan to photograph all of them.</td>', 'Congrats on a decent placing with a good photograph. After researching that region more after our hike I see there are many, many other equally fascinating places to photograph in the immediate area... I plan to photograph all of them.', '2009-07-09 04:17:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566482, 801477, 30214, '<td valign="top">I''ve seen it before, but nice to see it again! And congrats on The Blue! :)</td>', 'I''ve seen it before, but nice to see it again! And congrats on The Blue! :)', '2009-07-09 04:58:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566499, 802265, 30982, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous, Brian - very striking and strong composition, and a great catch of the colors.  I like the very faint second one, too.</td>', 'Gorgeous, Brian - very striking and strong composition, and a great catch of the colors.  I like the very faint second one, too.', '2009-07-09 07:07:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566500, 802966, 30982, '<td valign="top">Fascinating and lovely architecture.  Sadly, the vast majority probably didn''t pause long enough to appreciate the intricacies - like the neat swirl pattern in the floor formed by the reflections.  Very nice flow to this - neat place to photograph!</td>', 'Fascinating and lovely architecture.  Sadly, the vast majority probably didn''t pause long enough to appreciate the intricacies - like the neat swirl pattern in the floor formed by the reflections.  Very nice flow to this - neat place to photograph!', '2009-07-09 07:09:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566501, 803546, 30982, '<td valign="top">Awww - sweet!!  And I like the repeating forms of triangles throughout.</td>', 'Awww - sweet!!  And I like the repeating forms of triangles throughout.', '2009-07-09 07:10:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566502, 803593, 30982, '<td valign="top">I think you''ve received a lot of good feedback from your post to the forums - I''ll just say that I really liked their expressions and got a kick out of the bubbles!</td>', 'I think you''ve received a lot of good feedback from your post to the forums - I''ll just say that I really liked their expressions and got a kick out of the bubbles!', '2009-07-09 07:12:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566503, 802507, 30982, '<td valign="top">Reminds of the shoot out at the OK Corral - is this a re-enactment of that?  Though I didn''t know they had a photographer there!  The tones you used seem to suit this well, though a more tradition sepia might work well, too.</td>', 'Reminds of the shoot out at the OK Corral - is this a re-enactment of that?  Though I didn''t know they had a photographer there!  The tones you used seem to suit this well, though a more tradition sepia might work well, too.', '2009-07-09 07:15:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566504, 797364, 30982, '<td valign="top">Wow - that is a mess!  This is an excellent photojournalism type of shot - you''ve done a good job capturing the scene, I think.  Crisp, clear, shows the aftermath with enough of a view to see what happened but close enough to show some details.  Nice work!</td>', 'Wow - that is a mess!  This is an excellent photojournalism type of shot - you''ve done a good job capturing the scene, I think.  Crisp, clear, shows the aftermath with enough of a view to see what happened but close enough to show some details.  Nice work!', '2009-07-09 07:16:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566505, 803536, 30982, '<td valign="top">I keep wanting to call this "ways of seeing" but that may be a title from some other picture I viewed recently.  Not sure what you "fixed" as far as exposure, nor does it matter, as whatever it is you did seems to have worked quite well.  She''s leaving him, for the umpteenth time, but this time she means it, as he stares off into the distance, knowing that of course she''ll be back...</td>', 'I keep wanting to call this "ways of seeing" but that may be a title from some other picture I viewed recently.  Not sure what you "fixed" as far as exposure, nor does it matter, as whatever it is you did seems to have worked quite well.  She''s leaving him, for the umpteenth time, but this time she means it, as he stares off into the distance, knowing that of course she''ll be back...', '2009-07-09 07:24:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566506, 800379, 30982, '<td valign="top">Excellent work with the exposure on this in my opinion, and I really like the curious pose of the horse.  My only nit would be it seems to be a bit oversharpened - probably the sharpen edges thing.  (Then again, I''m not an oversharp kinda person.)</td>', 'Excellent work with the exposure on this in my opinion, and I really like the curious pose of the horse.  My only nit would be it seems to be a bit oversharpened - probably the sharpen edges thing.  (Then again, I''m not an oversharp kinda person.)', '2009-07-09 07:26:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566509, 802830, 30982, '<td valign="top">I know you''ve been doing the strobist kinda thing - I''m hoping to find a human or two to try it myself, but until then I''ll just be looking at what others are doing and taking notes...  I trust your aim was a low key''ish kinda thing here, and while I think it''s close, I''m not sure it''s quite there.  I can''t offer any help with it, though.  I quite like the light on the right side (as viewed) but on the left I''d have preferred it left a bit darker - as it is now, I can see a lot of grain/color noise, probably from trying to pull something out that was underexposed.</td>', 'I know you''ve been doing the strobist kinda thing - I''m hoping to find a human or two to try it myself, but until then I''ll just be looking at what others are doing and taking notes...  I trust your aim was a low key''ish kinda thing here, and while I think it''s close, I''m not sure it''s quite there.  I can''t offer any help with it, though.  I quite like the light on the right side (as viewed) but on the left I''d have preferred it left a bit darker - as it is now, I can see a lot of grain/color noise, probably from trying to pull something out that was underexposed.', '2009-07-09 07:33:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566510, 801885, 30982, '<td valign="top">Nifty place, nice processing to bring out it''s character!</td>', 'Nifty place, nice processing to bring out it''s character!', '2009-07-09 07:34:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566512, 802905, 30982, '<td valign="top">Beautiful portrait of the two of them!  Nice work with the focus, framing.  I''m betting she loves this shot!</td>', 'Beautiful portrait of the two of them!  Nice work with the focus, framing.  I''m betting she loves this shot!', '2009-07-09 07:35:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566518, 802521, 30982, '<td valign="top">A nice simple but very effective shot - very clean and crisp!  Would actually make a pretty good ad for FedEx.</td>', 'A nice simple but very effective shot - very clean and crisp!  Would actually make a pretty good ad for FedEx.', '2009-07-09 07:47:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566520, 803638, 30982, '<td valign="top">I referred to this as "Red Rock West" (interesting movie if you''ve not seen it) in a comment on one of Don''s shots - I think the two of these (yours and his) make a nice pairing.</td>', 'I referred to this as "Red Rock West" (interesting movie if you''ve not seen it) in a comment on one of Don''s shots - I think the two of these (yours and his) make a nice pairing.', '2009-07-09 07:48:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566522, 803017, 30982, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous colors in this and a pretty darn nice score in a FS!  Did I see this before in the flowers side challenge?  I ask because I seem to think I commented on it, but one doesn''t show here.</td>', 'Gorgeous colors in this and a pretty darn nice score in a FS!  Did I see this before in the flowers side challenge?  I ask because I seem to think I commented on it, but one doesn''t show here.', '2009-07-09 07:50:18.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(5566524, 797073, 52549, '<td valign="top">Wow, what an amazing image. Great work, Andrew.</td>', 'Wow, what an amazing image. Great work, Andrew.', '2009-07-09 07:51:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566525, 803162, 30982, '<td valign="top">LOL!  I LOVE the perspective on this!  And you had a very photogenic subject - he even has his hair styled nicely for the occasion and let the whiskers grow a touch for that more "manly" look.  Nicely done!  Not sure I want to hear the story about the deer.  :(</td>', 'LOL!  I LOVE the perspective on this!  And you had a very photogenic subject - he even has his hair styled nicely for the occasion and let the whiskers grow a touch for that more "manly" look.  Nicely done!  Not sure I want to hear the story about the deer.  :(', '2009-07-09 07:52:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566526, 798139, 52549, '<td valign="top">Super image, Anna. Congrats on your good finish.</td>', 'Super image, Anna. Congrats on your good finish.', '2009-07-09 07:55:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566527, 803172, 30982, '<td valign="top">I really like this!  I think the processing suits the shot well, and I really like the partial grin inside the bubble.  Not sure why having some of your choices be from your point and shoot makes any difference, unless you lost the originals?</td>', 'I really like this!  I think the processing suits the shot well, and I really like the partial grin inside the bubble.  Not sure why having some of your choices be from your point and shoot makes any difference, unless you lost the originals?', '2009-07-09 07:56:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566529, 803511, 52549, '<td valign="top">Love this, it''s fantastic. Also like the border, it all goes well together.</td>', 'Love this, it''s fantastic. Also like the border, it all goes well together.', '2009-07-09 07:56:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566539, 801474, 30982, '<td valign="top">Wow - exceptionally crisp and clean!  And great look from your subject, too.</td>', 'Wow - exceptionally crisp and clean!  And great look from your subject, too.', '2009-07-09 08:14:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566540, 799677, 30982, '<td valign="top">Excellent view of the place!  I love the light in this, the activity, the richness of the colors - you picked the right time of day.  Very nicely done, in my opinion!</td>', 'Excellent view of the place!  I love the light in this, the activity, the richness of the colors - you picked the right time of day.  Very nicely done, in my opinion!', '2009-07-09 08:16:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566541, 803272, 30982, '<td valign="top">Heh!  Should have known it was you from the title alone!  :-)  Looks a bit like Topaz on crispy setting.</td>', 'Heh!  Should have known it was you from the title alone!  :-)  Looks a bit like Topaz on crispy setting.', '2009-07-09 08:17:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5566542, 801831, 30982, '<td valign="top">I rather like the negative space.  And the wisp of cloud or steam or whatever that appears to be a transmission from the crane to the building.  I think they''re up to something....</td>', 'I rather like the negative space.  And the wisp of cloud or steam or whatever that appears to be a transmission from the crane to the building.  I think they''re up to something....', '2009-07-09 08:18:58.000000', NULL, 0),
