(5580976, 801254, 76335, '<td valign="top"><i>I''ve heard that "street" shots don''t do well in Free Studies but I liked this shot so here goes...</i> <br/> <br/>Well, now you know (!). Truly a 5.1 isn''t bad for a street shot in a FS. The players and spectators are clearly engaged, but it lacks a real "wow" factor necessary for a high score. I gave it a six. <br/> <br/>The background is fine. It needs that context. People who are distracted by distant signs or a few blown highlights have completely missed the point. I don''t mind a few imperfections in a street shot as long as the message is strong and it''s an honest capture. <br/> <br/>Keep at it.</td>', 'I''ve heard that "street" shots don''t do well in Free Studies but I liked this shot so here goes...  Well, now you know (!). Truly a 5.1 isn''t bad for a street shot in a FS. The players and spectators are clearly engaged, but it lacks a real "wow" factor necessary for a high score. I gave it a six.  The background is fine. It needs that context. People who are distracted by distant signs or a few blown highlights have completely missed the point. I don''t mind a few imperfections in a street shot as long as the message is strong and it''s an honest capture.  Keep at it.', '2009-07-20 21:36:29.000000', NULL, 0),
